Build lilv on the system serd, sord and sratom

Carla's lilv module compiles its fork of lilv 0.24 together with copies of
serd 0.24, sord 0.16 and sratom 0.6. Compile only lilv.c, and take serd,
sord and sratom from pkg-config: LILV_FLAGS for every compilation, since
CarlaLv2Utils.hpp includes sratom/sratom.h and is used throughout, and
LILV_LIBS wherever lilv.a is linked, which now includes the LV2 UI bridges.
The lilv fork itself stays: its API differs from upstream lilv.

Carla's serd patches are lost with its copy: one escapes '#' in file URIs,
which serd already does for the escaped URIs Carla builds, and one accepts
Turtle with a missing ';' or '.'.

Upstream: not submitted (upstream bundles its dependencies)
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/source/Makefile.deps.mk b/source/Makefile.deps.mk
